  "title": "Answer: the unified, controlling self may be a product of theorizing",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "629ce7a1-4214-44df-af6f-587cca7cab73",
      "text": "The self as a unified controller is part of the folk conception under revision. Split-brain and dissociation findings suggest control is distributed, and that the unified self may be a product of theorizing learned with language. Whether that is so is an empirical question.",
